@startuml hot-spot-distribution
title US-12: Live H3 Candidate Distribution - Redis Spatial Index

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

participant "Position\nConsumer" as Consumer
database "Redis\ngeo-cell:A" as CellA
database "Redis\ngeo-cell:B" as CellB
database "Redis\ngeo-cell:C" as CellC
participant "Correlation\nWorker" as Correlation

note over Consumer
  Busy airspace or shipping lane.
  Each accepted live position is mapped to
  LIVE_H3_RESOLUTION independently from history indexing.
end note

Consumer -> CellA : ZADD score=last_seen_ms entity_A
Consumer -> CellB : ZADD score=last_seen_ms entity_B
Consumer -> CellC : ZADD score=last_seen_ms entity_C

note over CellA, CellC
  These are Redis sorted sets, not TimescaleDB chunks.
  Spatial distribution reduces the candidate population
  that must be considered for exact proximity checks.
end note

Correlation -> CellB : ZRANGEBYSCORE current cell\n(now - freshness) +inf
Correlation -> CellA : query neighboring k-ring cell
Correlation -> CellC : query neighboring k-ring cell

CellA --> Correlation : fresh candidate IDs
CellB --> Correlation : fresh candidate IDs
CellC --> Correlation : fresh candidate IDs

Correlation -> Correlation : fetch live positions\nrecheck freshness\ncompute exact distance

note over Correlation
  k-ring radius is computed from
  PROXIMITY_THRESHOLD_METRES and
  LIVE_H3_RESOLUTION.
  Exact distance remains the anomaly criterion;
  H3 is only candidate reduction.
end note

@enduml
